# SwiftUI View Dependencies

See also [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for layer ownership. See [docs/ENGINEERING_DECISIONS.md](../../docs/ENGINEERING_DECISIONS.md) D13 for repository protocol status.

## Principle

A View depends on its presentation layer — nothing else.

A View's only business-facing dependency is its **ViewModel** or **Presentation Model** (`*Model`, `*ViewModel`).

Infrastructure (Store, Repository, Service, Provider) belongs outside the View tree.

---

## A View MAY Hold

- `@Bindable var model` / `let model` — the feature's ViewModel or Presentation Model.
- `@State` for **UI-only** ephemeral state (sheet visibility, focus, animation phase, raw search field text before debounce).
- Value types passed in for rendering (formatted strings, row snapshots, IDs used only for layout identity).
- Child views and Design System components.

---

## A View MUST NOT Hold

- `@Environment` of a Store, Repository, Service, or Provider.
- Stored properties typed as Store, Repository, Service, or Provider.
- Initializer parameters used to **construct** a ViewModel inside the View (e.g. `init(repository:transactionID:)` inside a View).
- Domain models used as the source of truth for mutation (pass presentation state instead).

If a View needs a Store to exist, it is the wrong place to create the ViewModel.

---

## Composition Root

Only the **composition root** may access infrastructure and construct ViewModels:

- `App` / root container views that own `@State` stores.
- Navigation destinations that receive infrastructure and inject a ready-made model.

```swift
// Composition root — allowed
.navigationDestination(for: Transaction.ID.self) { id in
    TransactionDetailView(
        model: TransactionDetailModel(repository: store, transactionID: id)
    )
}

// Feature view — required shape
struct TransactionDetailView: View {
    @Bindable var model: TransactionDetailModel

    var body: some View { /* layout only */ }
}
```

---

## Child Views

Private subviews (`*Content`, row views, field groups) follow the same rule:

- Consume `@Bindable var model`, presentation value types, or `@Binding` from the parent model.
- Never re-introduce Store/Repository access at a lower level.

---

## Code Smells

Reject or refactor when a View contains any of:

```swift
@Environment(TransactionStore.self) private var store
@Environment(SomeRepository.self) private var repository

init(store: TransactionStore, …) { … }

private var filteredItems: [Item] {
    store.items.filter { … }  // business query in View
}
```

---

## Previews

Previews construct infrastructure **outside** the View under test, then inject a model:

```swift
#Preview {
    TransactionDetailView(
        model: TransactionDetailModel(
            repository: PreviewTransactionStore.make(),
            transactionID: PreviewData.sampleTransactionID
        )
    )
}
```

Do not rely on `.environment(store)` to wire feature views in previews.

---

## Design Goal

Open a View file and see **layout + model** — never **layout + store**.

Dependency direction: `Infrastructure → ViewModel → View`.
